{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Read-to-Write Mismatch.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Read-to-Write Mismatch.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"read to write mismatch read to write mismatch","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Read-to-Write Mismatch.md","fileName":"Read-to-Write Mismatch.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Read-to-Write Mismatch","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-22 20:53\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[CQRS Query and Read Model Design]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["CQRS Query and Read Model Design","Aggregate","Command Query Responsibility Segregation","CQRS Command Model","CQRS Query Model","hands-ondomain-drivendesignwithnetcore.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Read-to-Write Mismatch.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Read-to-Write Mismatch.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"read to write mismatch read to write mismatch","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Read-to-Write Mismatch.md","fileName":"Read-to-Write Mismatch.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Read-to-Write Mismatch","heading":"Read-to-Write Mismatch","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"Read-to-write mismatch occurs when one representation and storage design cannot serve state changes and information retrieval equally well. Write models favor short transactions and invariant protection, while screens and reports may need joins, indexes, or fields drawn from several [[Aggregate]]s. Optimizing one side can degrade the other. [[Command Query Responsibility Segregation]] accepts this asymmetry by allowing the [[CQRS Command Model]] and [[CQRS Query Model]] to use different shapes without requiring separate databases immediately.","tags":["baby"],"links":["CQRS Query and Read Model Design","Aggregate","Command Query Responsibility Segregation","CQRS Command Model","CQ